# tally 2.1.8 R15 (#184), L §5.18: bal(x, d) from t is a balance, linear as the plain one is: the projection's
# start (9 999.00 PLN, its base's balance at t) is the known part, the February leg's hole its term.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input dom: int
input hamt[m in months]: money PLN
place k2: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

move hm[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  leg cash from k2 to world amount hamt[m]

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 5 "s"
  hamt[2026-01] = 1.00 PLN "s"
  hamt[2026-02] = ?"how much in Feb" "s"
  hamt[2026-03..2026-12] = 1.00 PLN "s"
  opening[k2] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask p4: bal(k2, 2026-02-28) from 2026-01-15 partial
ask p4b: bal(k2, 2026-03-31) from 2026-01-15 - bal(k2, 2026-01-31) partial
=== expect
p4: 9 999.00 PLN + -1 × ?"how much in Feb" (hamt[2026-02])
  cut 2026-01-01
p4b: -1.00 PLN + -1 × ?"how much in Feb" (hamt[2026-02])
  cut 2026-01-01
